h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 597)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Opening media with every window closed.</b> With no window open, File &#9656; Open Media or Session, Open Recent, and New Tab all work again: they make a window and load into it. The Dock icon now accepts movies, images, and folders too, so you can drop a folder of QuickTimes or an image sequence on Asobi and it opens the contents. Asobi never becomes the default app for those files.</li>
<li><b>Web review: the parked frame keeps its grade.</b> When a web viewer pauses, the full-resolution frame the host sends now carries the current grade, so the picture no longer appears to lose its color a second after stopping. Changing the grade while a viewer is parked refreshes their frame.</li>
<li>After this update, the tabs you had open may not come back the first time Asobi launches. That is a one-time effect of the change above.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
